00:41:13.700 --> 00:41:18.580
You get 15% off for good behavior, right?

00:41:18.580 --> 00:41:21.260
That brings you down to 34 months.

00:41:21.260 --> 00:41:26.260
And then you get six months of home confinement

00:41:26.620 --> 00:41:31.620
and you get another six months of halfway house time.

00:41:32.060 --> 00:41:36.620
Daniel had a problem with alcohol.

00:41:36.620 --> 00:41:39.700
If you can enroll in what's called the RDAP program,

00:41:39.700 --> 00:41:41.900
Residential Alcohol and Drug Program,

00:41:41.900 --> 00:41:44.660
they take another 12 months off your sentence.

00:41:44.660 --> 00:41:46.900
I said, dude, you're gonna do less than two years.

00:41:46.900 --> 00:41:48.420
So what did they do to screw him?

00:41:48.420 --> 00:41:52.020
Which is, you know, they just has a matter of policy.

00:41:52.020 --> 00:41:54.460
They screw every whistleblower in prison.

00:41:54.500 --> 00:41:57.140
The judge ordered that he be sent

00:41:57.140 --> 00:42:01.180
to a low security prison at Butner, North Carolina.

00:42:01.180 --> 00:42:02.820
That Butner is the national,

00:42:02.820 --> 00:42:07.260
it's the Bureau of Prisons National Prison Hospital Complex

00:42:07.260 --> 00:42:10.780
where Daniel could get treatment for very severe PTSD

00:42:10.780 --> 00:42:13.460
as you might have guessed,

00:42:13.460 --> 00:42:16.540
and also for an alcohol problem.

00:42:16.540 --> 00:42:18.460
One of the things that I learned the hard way

00:42:18.460 --> 00:42:20.620
is that when the judge makes an order like that,

